'''Vidara Jurness''' was a [[humanoid]] [[Vidara Jurness' species|alien]] [[mercenary]] who worked in the [[Black Mask]] gang alongside the [[human]] mercenary [[Vect Nokru]] and the mercenary [[Ayo Bons]], operating out of [[Daiyu City]] on the [[planet]] [[Daiyu]]. In [[9 BBY]], the gang was hired by the [[Reva Sevander|Third Sister]], an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Inquisitor]], to [[Ambush on Alderaan|kidnap]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], [[princess]] of the planet [[Alderaan]]. Having caught Organa in the [[forest]]s of Alderaan, they [[Prisoner|imprisoned]] her on their [[Unidentified mercenary starship|ship]] and brought her to the planet Daiyu. As the Third Sister expected, former [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] came to rescue Leia. At first, the mercenaries&mdash;including Jurness&mdash;managed to capture Kenobi, but the Jedi escaped by taking out the mercenaries with a [[spice]] he had obtained earlier.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Hello, Princess.''"<br />"''Why are you here?''"<br />"''Just waiting.''"<br />"''For what?''"<br />"''For you.|Vect Nokru and Princess Leia Organa, on Alderaan|<ref name="Part I" />}}
[[File:Falleen_Mercenary_chasing_Leia.png|thumb|left|300px|Jurness chases Leia]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], Vidara Jurness worked with the [[human]] [[mercenary]] [[Vect Nokru]] and the mercenary [[Ayo Bons]] as part of the [[Black Mask]] gang, which operated out of [[Daiyu City]]<ref name="Dawn Guide" /> on planet [[Daiyu]].<ref name="Part II">{{Kenobi|Part II}}</ref> In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Kenobi Date">{{KenobiDate|I}}</ref> the gang was hired by the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Inquisitor]] known as the [[Reva Sevander|Third Sister]] to [[Ambush on Alderaan|kidnap]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], [[princess]] of<ref name="Part I" /> the [[Core Worlds]] [[planet]]<ref name="Dawn Guide" /> [[Alderaan]]. The real goal of the Inquisitor was to lure [[Jedi]]-in-hiding [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] into a trap, expecting<ref name="Part I" /> the [[Alderaanian]] [[senator]]<ref name="Dawn Guide" /> [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] to ask the former [[Jedi Master]] to save his [[Gender|daughter]]. After traveling to Alderaan, the group waited for Leia in the [[forest]] and successfully captured her after shooting an [[Alderaan Guard|Alderaan guard]] in a short chase. Jurness then pulled a bag over Leia's head. After holding her hostage aboard their [[Unidentified mercenary starship|ship]],<ref name="Part I" /> Nokru contacted the Third Sister after brushing off counsel from the mercenary.<ref name="Topps 19">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi|cardname=19 - The Third Sister Orchestrates Leia's Kidnapping|link=https://www.tcdb.com/viewcard.cfm/sid/363350/cid/21461402}}</ref> Following this, the mercenaries took Leia to [[The Den]], a shady business in Daiyu City, and locked her in a cell.<ref name="Part II" />

[[File:NokruKenobi-OWKpII.png|thumb|right|300px|Jurness and her colleagues, pinning Kenobi to a wall]]
After their arrival on Daiyu, the group waited for Kenobi, who&mdash;as the Third Sister had expected&mdash;had been asked by Bail to save his daughter, to arrive. Once Kenobi had [[Search for Princess Leia|entered]] their hideout, the three ambushed him and managed to pin the Jedi against the wall while threatening him with their [[blaster]]s. Jurness then took Kenobi's [[Obi-Wan Kenobi's third lightsaber|lightsaber]] and handed it to Nokru, who was having a talk with Kenobi about how he had become vulnerable. However, Kenobi fled by taking out the mercenaries with [[spice]] he had obtained earlier.<ref name="Part II" /> The mercenaries were left locked in their own cell<ref name="Topps 25">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi|cardname=25 - Vect Nokru|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/363350/cid/21461408}}</ref> as they writhed in pain&mdash;enveloped by spice dust&mdash;until Third Sister arrived to demand where Kenobi was.<ref name="Topps 27">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi|cardname=27 - The Imposing Third Sister|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/363350/cid/21461410}}</ref> Sometime after Kenobi and Leia's escape, Jurness escaped from the cell and cleaned<ref name="Part II" /> her<ref name="Part I Audio" /> blaster. The Third Sister approached Nokru to put a [[bounty]] on the Jedi and inform all [[bounty hunter]]s on the planet about Kenobi's presence, although the princess and Jedi were ultimately able to escape Daiyu.<ref name="Part II" />

==Personality and traits==
Vidara Jurness was a [[humanoid]] [[Vidara Jurness' species|alien]] who had [[Color|green]], scaled skin and black [[hair]] that she kept styled in a ponytail.<ref name="Part I" />

==Skills and abilities==
Before the gang's attempt to kidnap Leia Organa on the patrolled grounds<ref name="Part I" /> of the [[Royal Palace of Alderaan]],<ref name="Part I Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/obi-wan-kenobi/part-i-guide|text=Part I Episode Guide &#124; Obi-Wan Kenobi}}</ref> Jurness showed her skill of remaining undetected.<ref name="Part I" />

==Equipment==
The mercenary was equipped with a blaster. She wore a long-sleeved, black [[Clothing|top]], a gray-brown sleeveless [[jacket]] with three cylinders and an electronic device on the front, black pants, a [[belt]] with a [[holster]] for her blaster, and black [[boot]]s. The crew of the three mercenaries also had a [[starship]].<ref name="Part I/>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Director Deborah Chow was such a joy to work with, and Ewin McGregor ''[sic]'' was an absolute gem of a person. Coordinator JoJo Eusebio held it down! And the team was full of energy and badassery.|Amy Sturdivant on the filming of ''Kenobi''|<ref name="Insta Post">{{Instagram|username=amy_sturdivant|url=p/CfMlR3IJytF|name=[[Amy Sturdivant]]|date=2022-06-24|archivedate=20221204194646}}</ref>}}
Vidara Jurness first appeared, albeit unidentified, in "[[Part I]]," the first episode of the [[Disney+]] live-action television series [[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi|''Obi-Wan Kenobi'']],<ref name="Part I" /> which premiered on [[May 27]], [[2022]].<ref name="Part I Premiere">{{SW|url=news/obi-wan-kenobi-may-27|text=''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' to Premiere May 27 with Two Episodes}}</ref> She is portrayed by [[Amy Sturdivant]],<ref name="Part I" /> whose previous ''[[Star Wars]]'' roles include serving as a stunt double for the mercenary [[Carasynthia Dune]] in the Disney+ television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''<ref name="Chapter 4">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 4: Sanctuary}}</ref> and potraying a [[clone trooper]] and a [[stormtrooper]] in ''Obi-Wan Kenobi''{{'s}} other episodes. She particularly enjoyed working with the show's director, [[Deborah Chow]]; Kenobi's actor, [[Ewan McGregor]]; and stunt director [[Jonathan (Jojo) Eusebio|Jojo Eusebio]]. The alien's scaly skin was applied to Sturdivant during filming via a layer on top of the actress's skin.<ref name="Insta Post" /> Jurness was first identified in the [[2023]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''<ref name="Dawn Guide" /> within a section written by [[Emily Shkoukani]].<ref name="DawnAuthor">{{WookYouTube|-nqSqVOvfM4|Wookieepedia Interviews - Emily Shkoukani & Jason Fry}}</ref>

